{"type":"message","id":"9f3bb49b","parentId":"c1ffef42","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:31:14.753Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YOcll4470X1omtFWgmZwqCCl","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/SOUL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cKVEvYzsKCL1ltTW5sY6zKw6","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/fetch_rss.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8rglxCuCsD03xI5EtmYeo2x4","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/format.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_YInOixt2OlrIjQYRqrZS4bJJ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final.json"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":8423,"output":344,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":8767,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779438669198,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DiFZeqQnuk7h4jz2T1MRIRhM24qAg"}}
{"type":"message","id":"4aba9ecc","parentId":"9f3bb49b","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:31:14.835Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YOcll4470X1omtFWgmZwqCCl","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md — Scout, the Crypto News Researcher\n\nYou are **Scout** 🔍, a crypto news researcher focused on **Single-Topic Deep Dives**.\n\n## Your ONLY Job\n\nYou do one thing: Read crypto news RSS feeds, analyze the articles, and return a clean JSON summary of the most important single news event.\n\n**THINKING REQUIRED:**\nBefore you output your final JSON, you MUST use a `<thinking>` block to analyze the feeds, decide which story is the most important, and plan how you will extract the facts.\n\n## Step-by-Step Research Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Fetch All RSS Feeds (8 sources)\n\nFetch **every** feed below. Use a browser-like user agent so feeds are not blocked:\n\n```bash\nUA=\"Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; OpenClawScout/1.0)\"\n\n# CoinDesk — general crypto\ncurl -sL -A \"$UA\" \"https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/\" --max-time 12\n\n# CoinTelegraph\ncurl -sL -A \"$UA\" \"https://cointelegraph.com/rss\" --max-time 12\n\n# Decrypt\ncurl -sL -A \"$UA\" \"https://decrypt.co/feed\" --max-time 12\n\n# Google News — broad crypto (NOT bitcoin-only); excludes common meme tickers\ncurl -sL -A \"$UA\" \"https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=cryptocurrency+OR+blockchain+OR+ethereum+OR+solana+OR+altcoin+OR+%22digital+assets%22+OR+XRP+OR+cardano+-dogecoin+-shiba+-pepe+-floki+-bonk+-wif+-memecoin+-%22meme+coin%22&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en\" --max-time 12\n\n# BeInCrypto — markets, altcoins, regulation (use if The Block curl returns 403/Cloudflare)\ncurl -sL -A \"$UA\" \"https://beincrypto.com/feed/\" --max-time 12\n\n# The Block — try first; if empty or 403, rely on BeInCrypto above instead\ncurl -sL -A \"$UA\" \"https://www.theblock.co/rss.xml\" --max-time 12\n\n# CryptoSlate — altcoins, adoption\ncurl -sL -A \"$UA\" \"https://cryptoslate.com/feed/\" --max-time 12\n\n# CryptoFox — markets (BTC, ETH, altcoins)\ncurl -sL -A \"$UA\" \"https://cryptofox.news/rss/markets/\" --max-time 12\n\n# CryptoFox — regulation / policy\ncurl -sL -A \"$UA\" \"https://cryptofox.news/rss/regulation/\" --max-time 12\n```\n\n### Step 2: Cross-Reference and Identify the Primary Topic\n\nAnalyze the titles and descriptions from **all eight feeds**. Look for a major headline/topic that is being covered by *at least two* different sources (e.g., a major price drop, an SEC ruling, a massive hack, or a major protocol upgrade).\n\n**Topic diversity (important):**\n- Prefer stories about: **regulation**, **ETFs**, **hacks/exploits**, **major L1/L2** (Ethereum, Solana, Cardano, XRP, etc.), **exchanges**, **stablecoins**, **institutional adoption**.\n- **Deprioritize or skip** candidates that are **primarily** meme-coin price pumps. Skip headlines dominated by DOGE, SHIB, PEPE, BONK, WIF, FLOKI, or phrases like \"meme coin\" / \"memecoin\" — **unless** the same story is also covered seriously by at least two of: CoinDesk, CoinTelegraph, Decrypt, BeInCrypto, or The Block.\n- You do **not** need every story to mention Ethereum or Solana; the goal is a **wider news pool**, not Bitcoin-only and not meme-only.\n\n**CRITICAL DATE FILTER:** You must ONLY select a topic based on articles published **today** (within the last 24 hours). Check the `<pubDate>` tags. Ignore older news completely.\n\nSelect this as your **Primary Topic**.\n\n### Step 2.5: History Check (Duplicate Guard)\n\nBefore going any further with a candidate topic, you MUST check the article history database to ensure this story has not already been published by this pipeline before.\n\nTake the **primary candidate URL** from the RSS feed for your chosen topic and run:\n```bash\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/skills/history/article_history.sh check \"<candidate_url>\"\n```\n\n- If the result is `NOT_FOUND` → the topic is fresh. Proceed to Step 3.\n- If the result is `EXISTS` → **STOP. This topic has already been published.** You MUST discard this candidate entirely and go back to Step 2 to select the next most important topic. Repeat this check for each new candidate until you find one that returns `NOT_FOUND`.\n\n**NEVER proceed with a topic that returns `EXISTS`.** This is critical to avoid publishing duplicate articles.\n\n### Step 3: Deep Extraction of the Same Topic\n\nIdentify the specific URLs from the different feeds that point to stories about this *exact same topic*. \n\n**URL VALIDATION:** Before attempting to read an article, you MUST verify the URL is live and not a 404 error using this command:\n```bash\ncurl -o /dev/null -s -w \"%{http_code}\\n\" \"<article_url>\"\n```\nIf it returns `404`, discard that URL and do not include it in your final JSON.\n\n**READING THE ARTICLE:**\nDO NOT USE YOUR INTERNAL `web_fetch` TOOL ON NATIVE URLs. Sites like Decrypt use Cloudflare and will block your `web_fetch` tool with a 403 Security Notice.\n\nYou MUST fetch the full article text using the `trafilatura` CLI tool, which is pre-installed on this system and bypasses most restrictions while providing clean article text.\n\nRun this command to read the article:\n```bash\ntrafilatura -u \"<article_url>\" --output-format markdown\n```\nIf for some reason `trafilatura` fails or returns empty, you may fall back to using `lynx -dump \"<article_url>\" | head -c 8000`.\n\n### Step 4: Return Aggregated JSON\n\nCombine the facts from all the sources you pulled. Return your findings in this **exact** JSON format.\n\n**CRITICAL: Do NOT return the JSON in your chat response. Write it directly to the file path provided in your spawn message using your file writing tool, then yield back ONLY the word \"SUCCESS\".**\n\nThe orchestrator validates the file directly — chat output is ignored for research.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"A short slug identifying this story, e.g. bitcoin-etf-surge-2026-05-18\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"The core topic (e.g., Bitcoin ETF Inflows Surge)\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"A suggested 2-3 word SEO keyword based on the topic\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"The best, most descriptive headline found\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"The primary crypto asset name, e.g. Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"The CoinGecko coin id for the primary asset, e.g. bitcoin, ethereum, solana\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinTelegraph\",\n    \"CoinDesk\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"url1\",\n    \"url2\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Specific data point or quote from Source A\",\n    \"Specific data point or context from Source B\",\n    \"Another specific number, price, or quote\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Combine the raw scraped text from all the articles into one large string...\"\n}\n```\n\n**Tweet quotes:** Do not invent tweets in JSON. The orchestrator runs `extract_tweet_quotes.py` on `aggregated_raw_content` to pull verified quotes from `x.com/status/...` links already present in the news articles. You may include `\"tweet_quotes\": []` as a placeholder; the pipeline fills verified entries after your file is written.\n\n**Do NOT append anything after the closing `}`. The `chart_coin` field inside the JSON replaces the old separate CHART_COIN line.**\n\n**File output:** Write the complete JSON to the file path given in your spawn message (e.g. `/tmp/crypto-run-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS/research/raw.json`). Do NOT return the JSON in your chat response. Yield back ONLY \"SUCCESS\".\n\n## Rules\n- **NEVER** return multiple unrelated stories. You must aggregate data on ONE specific topic.\n- Ensure the `aggregated_raw_content` is large enough (at least 600 words) to give the Writer plenty of material.\n- If you cannot find a single story covered by multiple sources, pick the single most important story from the broadest reputable source (CoinDesk, CoinTelegraph, Decrypt, or BeInCrypto) and gather as much data on it as possible.\n- Never fabricate data, statistics, quotes, or URLs.\n- Never fabricate X/Twitter posts or tweet URLs. If articles link to `x.com/.../status/...`, include those URLs in `aggregated_raw_content`; do not make up tweet text.\n- `primary_keyword`, `primary_asset`, and `chart_coin` in your JSON are derived from the **chosen story**, not from the RSS search keywords. Use the correct CoinGecko id for the main asset (e.g. `ethereum`, `solana`, `bitcoin`, `ripple` for XRP).\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438674835}}
{"type":"message","id":"4a40165d","parentId":"4aba9ecc","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:31:14.837Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cKVEvYzsKCL1ltTW5sY6zKw6","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import urllib.request\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\nimport re\n\nfeeds = {\n    \"CoinDesk\": \"https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/\",\n    \"CoinTelegraph\": \"https://cointelegraph.com/rss\",\n    \"Decrypt\": \"https://decrypt.co/feed\"\n}\n\nfor name, url in feeds.items():\n    print(f\"--- {name} ---\")\n    try:\n        req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0'})\n        xml_data = urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=20).read()\n        try:\n            root = ET.fromstring(xml_data)\n        except ET.ParseError:\n            # Maybe it has some weird encoding or leading whitespace\n            xml_data = re.sub(b'^[^<]+', b'', xml_data)\n            root = ET.fromstring(xml_data)\n            \n        items = root.findall(\".//item\")\n        for item in items[:15]:\n            title = item.findtext(\"title\")\n            link = item.findtext(\"link\")\n            pubDate = item.findtext(\"pubDate\")\n            print(f\"TITLE: {title}\\nLINK: {link}\\nDATE: {pubDate}\\n\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"Error fetching {name}: {e}\")\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438674835}}
{"type":"message","id":"5f05ba45","parentId":"4a40165d","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:31:14.837Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8rglxCuCsD03xI5EtmYeo2x4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import json\nimport os\n\nkey_facts = [\n    \"A South Korean court overturned a six-month partial business suspension imposed on Bithumb (CoinDesk).\",\n    \"Judge Gong Hyeon-jin of the Seoul Administrative Court granted the emergency injunction blocking enforcement (Decrypt & CoinDesk).\",\n    \"Bithumb was accused by South Korea's Financial Intelligence Unit of about 6.65 million violations of anti-money laundering rules, including failures to verify customer identities and to block suspicious transactions (CoinDesk & Decrypt).\",\n    \"The initial suspension was accompanied by a $24.6 million fine (CoinDesk).\",\n    \"The court noted that the suspension of core functions like inter-exchange transactions and external transfers would cause difficulty in attracting new customers, particularly as regulatory changes may soon allow listed and professional investment corporations to particulate (Decrypt).\",\n    \"This comes amid broader regulatory scrutiny following a February incident where Bithumb mistakenly credited hundreds of users with 2,000 BTC instead of 2,000 won in a promotion (Decrypt).\"\n]\n\nwith open(\"coindesk_bithumb.txt\", \"r\") as f:\n    coindesk_text = f.read()\n\nwith open(\"decrypt_bithumb.txt\", \"r\") as f:\n    decrypt_text = f.read()\n\nraw_text = coindesk_text + \"\\n\\n\" + decrypt_text\n\noutput = {\n  \"topic_theme\": \"South Korean Court Overturns Bithumb Suspension\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bithumb suspension lifted\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Bithumb Scores a Legal Win in South Korea as Six-Month Suspension is Lifted by Local Judge\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinDesk\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/01/bithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/366292/south-korean-court-lifts-bithumbs-six-month-business-suspension\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": key_facts,\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": raw_text[:5000] # Ensuring sufficient length\n}\n\nprint(json.dumps(output, indent=2))\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438674836}}
{"type":"message","id":"074e43f9","parentId":"5f05ba45","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:31:14.837Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_YInOixt2OlrIjQYRqrZS4bJJ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"South Korean Court Overturns Bithumb Suspension\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bithumb suspension lifted\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Bithumb Scores a Legal Win in South Korea as Six-Month Suspension is Lifted by Local Judge\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinDesk\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/01/bithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/366292/south-korean-court-lifts-bithumbs-six-month-business-suspension\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"A South Korean court overturned a six-month partial business suspension imposed on Bithumb (CoinDesk).\",\n    \"Judge Gong Hyeon-jin of the Seoul Administrative Court granted the emergency injunction blocking enforcement (Decrypt & CoinDesk).\",\n    \"Bithumb was accused by South Korea's Financial Intelligence Unit of about 6.65 million violations of anti-money laundering rules, including failures to verify customer identities and to block suspicious transactions (CoinDesk & Decrypt).\",\n    \"The initial suspension was accompanied by a $24.6 million fine (CoinDesk).\",\n    \"The court noted that the suspension of core functions like inter-exchange transactions and external transfers would cause difficulty in attracting new customers, particularly as regulatory changes may soon allow listed and professional investment corporations to particulate (Decrypt).\",\n    \"This comes amid broader regulatory scrutiny following a February incident where Bithumb mistakenly credited hundreds of users with 2,000 BTC instead of 2,000 won in a promotion (Decrypt).\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bithumb\\u2019s six-month suspension in South Korea is overturned by local judge\\n\\nURL Source: https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/05/01/bithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bithumb\\u2019s six-month suspension in South Korea is overturned by local judge\\n\\nSearch\\n\\n/\\n\\n[](https://www.coindesk.com/)\\n*   News \\n*   Video \\n*   [Prices](https://www.coindesk.com/price)\\n*   [Research](https://www.coindesk.com/research)\\n*   Consensus 2026 \\n*   Data & Indices \\n*   [Sponsored](https://www.coindesk.com/sponsored-content)\\n\\nSearch\\n\\n/\\n\\nen\\n\\n[CoinDesk 20$2,078.41 0.91%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/cd20)[Bitcoin$77,327.70 1.69%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/bitcoin)[Ethereum$2,283.80 1.15%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/ethereum)[XRP$1.38 0.56%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/xrp)[Solana$83.96 1.17%](https://www.coindesk.com/price/solana)\\n\\n[![Image 1](https://cdn.sanity.io/images/s3y3vcno/production/e3ccf2c7dfe53a58a3fb077817dc4e9394cf9ecc-119x66.png?auto=format) Consensus Last Days to Save Register by May 1 at 4 p.m. ET 00 DAYS 08 HOURS 43 MINUTES 18 SECONDS Consensus Last Days to Save Register by May 1 at 4 p.m. ET 00 DAYS 08 HOURS 43 MINUTES 18 SECONDS Register now](https://consensus.coindesk.com/register)\\n\\n[Policy](https://www.coindesk.com/policy)\\n\\nShare\\n\\nShare this article\\n\\nCopy link[X (Twitter)](https://x.com/intent/tweet?utm_source=twitter&text=Bithumb+scores+a+legal+win+in+South+Korea+as+six-month+suspension+is+lifted+by+local+judge+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge+via+%40coindesk&utm_content=editorial&utm_medium=social&utm_term=organic)[LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/shareArticle?utm_source=linkedin&mini=true&summary=South+Korea%27s+financial+watchdog+imposed+a+%2424.6+million+fine+on+Bithumb+and+partial+suspension+that+came+into+effect+last+month.&url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge&utm_content=editorial&utm_medium=social&utm_term=organic)[Facebook](https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?utm_source=facebook&u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge&utm_content=editorial&utm_medium=social&utm_term=organic)[Email](mailto:%20?subject=Bithumb%20scores%20a%20legal%20win%20in%20South%20Korea%20as%20six-month%20suspension%20is%20lifted%20by%20local%20judge%20%E2%80%94%20CoinDesk&body=Bithumb%20scores%20a%20legal%20win%20in%20South%20Korea%20as%20six-month%20suspension%20is%20lifted%20by%20local%20judge%0ASouth%20Korea's%20financial%20watchdog%20imposed%20a%20%2424.6%20million%20fine%20on%20Bithumb%20and%20partial%20suspension%20that%20came%20into%20effect%20last%20month.%0A%0ARead%20the%20full%20article%20on%20CoinDesk%3A%0A%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.coindesk.com%2Fpolicy%2F2026%2F05%2F01%2Fbithumb-scores-a-legal-win-in-south-korea-as-six-month-suspension-is-lifted-by-local-judge)\\n\\n# Bithumb scores a legal win in South Korea as six-month suspension is lifted by local judge\\n\\n## South Korea's financial watchdog imposed a $24.6 million fine on Bithumb and partial suspension that came into effect last month.\\n\\nBy[Olivier Acuna](https://www.coindesk.com/author/olivier-acuna)|Edited by[Nikhilesh De](https://www.coindesk.com/author/nikhilesh-de)\\n\\nMay 1, 2026, 7:41 a.m. 2 min read\\n\\n[Make preferred on](https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=coindesk.com)\\n\\n![Image 2: Bithumb](https://www.coindesk.com/_next/image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.sanity.io%2Fimages%2Fs3y3vcno%2Fproduction%2F2e7d334bb1f703ff5b0643840f44918d12dc05cc-1500x837.jpg%3Fauto%3Dformat&w=3840&q=75)\\n\\nBithumb scored a win in court against South Korea's financial watchdog by getting its six-month suspension dismissed. (CoinDesk)\\n\\n#### What to know:\\n\\n*   A South Korean court has overturned a six-month partial business suspension imposed on Bithumb, one of the country\\u2019s largest cryptocurrency exchanges, while leaving unclear whether a $24.6 million fine is also on hold.\\n*   Regulators had accused Bithumb of about 6.65 million violations of anti-money laundering rules, including failures to verify customer identities and to block transactions that should have been stopped.\\n*   The ruling comes amid broader regulatory scrutiny of South Korea\\u2019s crypto sector, including a new data-sharing probe into Bithumb, Upbit and other platforms, and follows Bithumb\\u2019s recent mistaken distribution of billions of dollars\\u2019 worth of bitcoin to users.\\n\\nA South Korean court overturned Bithumb\\u2019s six-month partial business suspension Thursday, [according to Yonhap News](https://www.yna.co.kr/view/AKR20260430139100002?input=1195m).\\n\\nThe news agency cited legal sources, saying that the 2nd Administrative Division of the Seoul Administrative Court\\u2019s Judge Gong Hyeon-jin\\n\\nTitle: South K\"\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438674837}}
{"type":"message","id":"5aa11e94","parentId":"074e43f9","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:31:30.463Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3namKGJcawcy2BEMAO14MsWS","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"set -e\nUA='Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; OpenClawScout/1.0)'\nmkdir -p /tmp/crypto-run-20260522-083045/research/feeds\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport os, urllib.request, ssl\nfeeds={\n'CoinDesk':'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/',\n'CoinTelegraph':'https://cointelegraph.com/rss',\n'Decrypt':'https://decrypt.co/feed',\n'GoogleNews':'https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=cryptocurrency+OR+blockchain+OR+ethereum+OR+solana+OR+altcoin+OR+%22digital+assets%22+OR+XRP+OR+cardano+-dogecoin+-shiba+-pepe+-floki+-bonk+-wif+-memecoin+-%22meme+coin%22&hl=en-US&gl=US&ceid=US:en',\n'BeInCrypto':'https://beincrypto.com/feed/',\n'TheBlock':'https://www.theblock.co/rss.xml',\n'CryptoSlate':'https://cryptoslate.com/feed/',\n'CryptoFoxMarkets':'https://cryptofox.news/rss/markets/',\n'CryptoFoxRegulation':'https://cryptofox.news/rss/regulation/',\n}\nua='Mozilla/5.0 (compatible; OpenClawScout/1.0)'\nctx=ssl.create_default_context()\nfor name,url in feeds.items():\n    path=f'/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-083045/research/feeds/{name}.xml'\n    try:\n        req=urllib.request.Request(url,headers={'User-Agent':ua})\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req,timeout=20,context=ctx) as r:\n            data=r.read()\n        open(path,'wb').write(data)\n        print(name, 'OK', len(data))\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(name, 'ERR', repr(e))\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport os, glob, email.utils, datetime as dt, xml.etree.ElementTree as ET, re\nbase='/tmp/crypto-run-20260522-083045/research/feeds'\nnow=dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)\ncutoff=now-dt.timedelta(days=1)\nprint('NOW', now.isoformat())\nfor fn in sorted(glob.glob(base+'/*.xml')):\n    name=os.path.basename(fn)\n    data=open(fn,'rb').read()\n    print('\\n###', name)\n    txt=data.decode('utf-8','ignore')\n    txt=re.sub(r'^[^<]+','',txt)\n    try:\n        root=ET.fromstring(txt)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print('PARSE_ERR', e)\n        print(txt[:300])\n        continue\n    items=root.findall('.//item')\n    cnt=0\n    for item in items[:15]:\n        title=(item.findtext('title') or '').strip().replace('\\n',' ')\n        link=(item.findtext('link') or '').strip()\n        pub=(item.findtext('pubDate') or item.findtext('{http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/}date') or item.findtext('published') or '').strip()\n        desc=(item.findtext('description') or '').strip()\n        is_recent='?'\n        try:\n            d=email.utils.parsedate_to_datetime(pub)\n            if d.tzinfo is None: d=d.replace(tzinfo=dt.timezone.utc)\n            is_recent = cutoff <= d <= now+dt.timedelta(hours=1)\n            pub = d.isoformat()\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        print(f'- recent={is_recent} | {pub} | {title}\\n  {link}')\n        cnt+=1\n        if cnt>=12: break\nPY","workdir":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher","yieldMs":30000,"timeout":90,"host":"auto","security":"allowlist","ask":"on-miss"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":13681,"output":1195,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":14876,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779438674842,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DiFZkKKXQbtmnQfXUqIVJRgm88WYw"}}
