{"type":"message","id":"bc262668","parentId":"f9eb6a4f","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:32:23.578Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_xjrJGxPU4VjULefFETBsNaO4","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_NE1mc3KDB5yTDnZQJyF8HfGd","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_summary.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_Mfo7vKyzXHpRdhtgVlSHUTnc","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/crypto_news_deep_dive.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_zP0WalNVUldnq1yJB5pYOKsC","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_output.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_mpL9Do2EJjyl2chX5Y4xC99n","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/final_report.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_kehEQt73q8RE8UawaWao7ij2","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-researcher/result.json"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":31664,"output":475,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32139,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779438734613,"responseId":"chatcmpl-DiFaioPlv9RDlRYEKZlgIgY0TApZM"}}
{"type":"message","id":"6a7b2bb6","parentId":"bc262668","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:32:23.725Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_xjrJGxPU4VjULefFETBsNaO4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"SBI Holdings' Potential Acquisition of Bitbank\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"SBI Bitbank acquisition\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"SBI to Make Bitbank a Subsidiary in Japan Crypto Consolidation Push\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinTelegraph\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-seeks-to-make-bitbank-a-subsidiary-in-japan-crypto-consolidation-push\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Tokyo-based SBI Holdings has opened talks to acquire shares in cryptocurrency exchange Bitbank and make it a consolidated subsidiary.\",\n    \"The move is part of SBI's push to consolidate regulated crypto trading platforms in Japan.\",\n    \"The potential deal would help the group establish an “overwhelming position in the domestic cryptocurrency industry.”\",\n    \"Japan’s Cabinet approved a bill on April 10 to amend the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act and the Payment Services Act, strengthening crypto market fairness, transparency, and investor protection.\",\n    \"Bitbank is one of Japan’s major crypto exchanges, ranking as the leading cryptocurrency exchange by Coingecko’s trust score.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: SBI to Make Bitbank a Subsidiary in Japan Crypto Consolidation Push\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-seeks-to-make-bitbank-a-subsidiary-in-japan-crypto-consolidation-push\\n\\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 11:17:45 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nTokyo-based SBI Holdings has opened talks to acquire shares in cryptocurrency exchange Bitbank and make it a consolidated subsidiary, extending its push to consolidate regulated crypto trading platforms in Japan as the country moves toward securities-style rules for digital assets.\\n\\nThe financial conglomerate [said](https://www.sbigroup.co.jp/news/2026/0501_16298.html) Friday it is considering a share acquisition as part of a potential capital and business alliance with Bitbank. The deal remains subject to due diligence, negotiations and internal approvals, SBI said.\\n\\nThe talks come a month after SBI VC Trade [absorbed](https://www.sbivc.co.jp/newsview/umhk6419ku) Bitpoint Japan on April 1, with SBI VC Trade becoming the surviving company. A Bitbank acquisition would give SBI a larger position in Japan’s crypto exchange market at a time when policymakers are preparing to bring crypto assets under the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act.\\n\\nSBI said the potential deal would help the group establish an “overwhelming position in the domestic cryptocurrency industry,” citing Japan’s planned regulatory shift for crypto assets.\\n\\nJapan’s Cabinet approved a bill on April 10 to [amend the Financial Instruments and Exchange Act](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-approves-bill-classify-cryptocurrencies-financial-instruments) and the Payment Services Act, according to the Financial Services Agency. The bill is intended to strengthen market fairness, transparency and investor protection while revising rules for crypto assets.\\n\\nCrypto assets are currently regulated by the FSA under the Payment Services Act as a means of payment. The proposed changes would move crypto closer to Japan’s traditional financial market framework, with stronger disclosure, exchange oversight and rules targeting unfair trading.\\n\\nCointelegraph asked SBI Holdings for comment on the proposed Bitbank acquisition and how Japan’s shifting crypto rules are affecting the group’s exchange strategy, but had not received a response by publication.\\n\\n![Image 1](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-222.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Bitbank company profile. Source: SBI Group_\\n\\nBitbank is one of Japan’s major crypto exchanges. It [ranks](https://www.coingecko.com/en/exchanges/country/japan) as Japan’s leading cryptocurrency exchange by Coingecko’s trust score, which measures the legitimacy of crypto exchanges based on liquidity, trading activity, cybersecurity and operational scale.\\n\\nIt ranks third among cryptocurrency exchanges by daily trading volume, behind bitFlyer and Coincheck.\\n\\n![Image 2](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/pasted-image-223.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Top Japanese crypto exchanges by trust score. Source: Coingecko_\\n\\nThe proposed deal would add to SBI’s broader digital asset footprint. SBI made a $50 million investment in Circle's IPO in June 2025. In previous years, SBI also made strategic investments in other crypto-native companies, including BITPoint Japan, Sygnum Bank and crypto exchange TaoTao, which later merged into SBI VC Trade.\\n\\n## Japan brings crypto under TradFi umbrella, targets ETFs by 2028\\n\\nJapan’s regulatory shift comes as institutional interest in digital assets continues to grow and policymakers reassess how crypto should fit within the country’s financial markets.\\n\\nJapanese Finance Minister Satsuki Katayama first [signaled](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-crypto-securities-framework-exchange-led-access-2026) the intent to bring crypto under the same umbrella as traditional finance assets in January, to ensure that citizens will “benefit from digital and blockchain-based assets.”\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**South Korea’s Shinhan Card taps Solana to test real-world stablecoin payments**_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/south-korean-credit-card-giant-partners-with-solana-for-stablecoin-payments-defi-infrastructure)\\n\\nThe country is also planning to legalize the launch of cryptocurrency exchange-traded funds (ETFs) by 2028, [according](https://cointelegraph.com/news/japan-considers-crypto-etfs-2028-nikkei) to a January report. Large financial conglomerates like SBI Holdings and Nomura are among the first companies expected to [develop crypto-linked ETFs](https://cointelegraph.com/news/sbi-plans-bitcoin-xrp-etf-japan).\\n\\n_**Magazine:**_[_**Singapore isn’t a ‘crypto hub’ — it’s something better: StraitsX CEO**_](https://cointelegraph-magazine.com/singapore-crypto-speculation-down-mas-loophole-closure-asia-express/)\\n\\nCointelegraph\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438743725}}
{"type":"message","id":"cac6c818","parentId":"6a7b2bb6","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:32:23.725Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_NE1mc3KDB5yTDnZQJyF8HfGd","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Bitcoin's April Rally Driven by Speculation, Posing Risk of Price Correction\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bitcoin price correction\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/366267/bitcoin-crash-incoming-april-surge-built-shaky-ground-analysts-warn\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"CryptoQuant analysis indicates Bitcoin's 20% April rally was 'driven entirely by growth in perpetual futures demand.'\",\n    \"Spot demand for Bitcoin contracted during the same period, suggesting the market's marginal buyer was 'speculative, not fundamental.'\",\n    \"The divergence between rising prices and falling spot demand is described as 'one of the clearest on-chain signals' that the gains are not structural.\",\n    \"CryptoQuant warns that this pattern of futures-driven rallies without spot demand has historically preceded 'extended periods of price declines.'\",\n    \"Bitcoin is currently trading around $77,000 after reaching a peak of $79,000 in April.\",\n    \"The market capitalization of Bitcoin saw a significant increase, but the underlying support from long-term investors or direct asset purchase appears weak.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\\n\\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 10:28:12 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin risks extended retreat as April rally was futures-driven: CryptoQuant\\n\\nFutures drove up Bitcoin's price in April while spot demand declined, which CryptoQuant warned has historically preceded extended price declines.\\n\\nBitcoin could be setting up for a multimonth price decline, after a rally in April driven mainly by futures traders while spot demand declined, according to the crypto analytics firm CryptoQuant.\\n\\nBitcoin gained around 20% in April, rising from $66,000 to a peak of $79,000 in a rally “driven entirely by growth in perpetual futures demand,” CryptoQuant said in a report on Thursday.\\n\\nMeanwhile, spot demand for Bitcoin contracted throughout the rally, “indicating that the market’s marginal buyer was speculative, not fundamental,” it said.\\n\\n“The divergence between rising price and contracting spot demand is one of the clearest on-chain signals that price gains are speculative rather than structural,” CryptoQuant added.\\n\\nBitcoin is trading around $77,000 at the time of writing, rising 2.1% over the past 24 hours.\\n\\nTitle: Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn\\n\\nURL Source: https://decrypt.co/366267/bitcoin-crash-incoming-april-surge-built-shaky-ground-analysts-warn\\n\\nPublished Time: 2026-04-30T20:30:19\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn - Decrypt\\n\\nThe recent surge in Bitcoin’s price, which saw it climb impressively throughout April, may not be as stable as it appears. Market analysts are pointing to underlying data that suggests the rally was built on speculative trading rather than solid, fundamental demand. Experts from analytics firm CryptoQuant have highlighted that the growth was predominantly fueled by perpetual futures contracts, a form of derivative trading that allows for high leverage. Simultaneously, on-chain data shows that actual spot-market buying—the direct purchase of Bitcoin—has been declining. This is a concerning divergence. When prices rise without the backing of genuine buying interest from long-term holders or new retail investors, it often creates a fragile market susceptible to sharp corrections. Historically, such patterns have often been the precursor to significant price drops, as the speculative fervor dies down and the lack of foundational support becomes apparent. While Bitcoin currently holds a strong position near its recent highs, investors are being warned to proceed with caution, as the shaky ground on which the April surge was built could give way, potentially leading to a market-wide crash.\"\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438743725}}
{"type":"message","id":"4a1c59de","parentId":"cac6c818","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:32:23.726Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Mfo7vKyzXHpRdhtgVlSHUTnc","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Canada Proposes Ban on Crypto ATMs\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Canada crypto ATM ban\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Canada proposes crypto ATM ban over scams and money laundering\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinDesk\",\n    \"Cointelegraph\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/04/29/canada-proposes-ban-on-bitcoin-atms-as-fraud-cases-mount\",\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/canada-proposes-crypto-atm-ban-over-scams-and-money-laundering\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"The proposal is part of the Liberal government's Spring Economic Update, aimed at combating fraud and money laundering.\",\n    \"Officials describe crypto ATMs as a 'primary method' for scammers to defraud victims and for criminals to launder the proceeds of crime.\",\n    \"The world’s first publicly available Bitcoin ATM went live in a Vancouver coffee shop in 2013, making Canada the birthplace of the technology.\",\n    \"Canada has the second-highest number of crypto ATMs globally, accounting for an estimated 10.1% of all installations.\",\n    \"The ban is part of a broader regulatory push that includes a new Financial Crimes Agency and stricter rules for money services businesses.\",\n    \"The government is also advancing legislation to bar the use of cryptocurrency for political donations over concerns about traceability.\",\n    \"A government investigation found that crypto ATMs are the principal method used by fraudsters to extract money from Canadian victims.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Canada proposes ban on BTC ATMs as fraud cases mount\\n\\nURL Source: https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/04/29/canada-proposes-ban-on-bitcoin-atms-as-fraud-cases-mount\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\n# Canada proposes ban on BTC ATMs as fraud cases mount\\n\\nCanada’s Liberal government has proposed a nationwide ban on bitcoin and other crypto ATMs as part of a broader effort to combat fraud and money laundering. Officials say crypto ATMs have become a “primary method” for scammers to defraud victims and for criminals to launder illicit cash, citing findings from the financial intelligence agency FINTRAC. The move comes as lawmakers also weigh banning crypto as a form of electoral donations, even though Canada hosted the world’s first bitcoin ATM in Vancouver in 2013. The measure, included in the Liberal government's Spring Economic Update released Tuesday, would eliminate crypto ATMs nationwide. Officials described the machines as a 'primary method' for defrauding victims and laundering illicit funds. 'To protect Canadians by shutting down a primary method for scammers to defraud victims, and for criminals to place their cash proceeds of crime,' the government said, it plans to prohibit the machines entirely. A crypto ATM (automated teller machine) may sound similar to a traditional cash machine that dispenses money from your bank account, but it works very differently. Instead of withdrawing cash, these machines let users convert physical cash into crypto.\\n\\nTitle: Canada Proposes Crypto ATM Ban to Tackle Scams, Money Laundering\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/canada-proposes-crypto-atm-ban-over-scams-and-money-laundering\\n\\nPublished Time: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 10:17:25 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nThe Canadian government has proposed banning Bitcoin and other crypto ATMs, arguing the machines have become a primary on-ramp for fraudsters and money launderers rather than a convenient access point for everyday users. The government's Spring Economic Update 2026, published on April 28, says crypto ATMs are a “primary method for scammers to defraud victims and for criminals to place their cash proceeds of crime,” and explicitly states that the government “proposes to ban crypto ATMs.” The proposal states that Canadians will still be able to buy virtual currencies from brick-and-mortar money services businesses, but the standalone kiosks that have proliferated in malls, gas stations and corner stores would be phased out. The move adds to a broader push by Ottawa to clamp down on what it frames as retail-facing crypto risks as fraud cases surge, while bringing more of the digital asset sector under tighter federal oversight. Authorities say the move is aimed at cutting off one of the most common channels used in scams that have increasingly targeted Canadians. The policy is of particular note given Canada’s early role in the sector. The world’s first publicly available Bitcoin ATM went live in a Vancouver coffee shop in 2013, making Canada the birthplace of the Bitcoin ATM. Since then, the country has grown into one of the most crypto-ATM-dense markets globally, a status regulators say has given it disproportionate exposure to fraud. Coin ATM Radar data estimates that Canada accounts for 10.1% of global crypto ATMs, second only to the United States. A months-long CBC investigation and internal Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada (FINTRAC) analysis posted April 28 found that crypto ATMs have become the principal method used by domestic and foreign criminal fraudsters to extract money from Canadian scam victims and push those funds into the crypto ecosystem. Law enforcement agencies told CBC they have seen a clear uptick in cases where victims are instructed to feed cash into these machines under the guise of paying tax debts, securing romance relationships or recovering hacked accounts. The proposed ATM ban sits within a broader effort to tighten controls around high-risk corners of Canada’s crypto market while drawing core infrastructure more firmly into the regulatory perimeter. The same Spring Economic Update bolsters a new Financial Crimes Agency and gives FINTRAC more tools to refuse or revoke registrations for non-compliant money services businesses, including crypto companies.\"\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779438743725}}
{"type":"message","id":"46399a04","parentId":"4a1c59de","timestamp":"2026-05-22T08:32:23.726Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_zP0WalNVUldnq1yJB5pYOKsC","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Bitcoin Price Correction Risk\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"Bitcoin futures rally\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Bitcoin risks extended retreat as April rally was futures-driven: CryptoQuant\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinTelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/366267/bitcoin-crash-incoming-april-surge-built-shaky-ground-analysts-warn\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"CryptoQuant warns that the recent Bitcoin price rally in April was primarily driven by the futures market, not an increase in spot demand.\",\n    \"A decline in the 'spot-to-futures volume ratio' suggests the rally was speculative and may not be sustainable.\",\n    \"Historically, similar patterns where futures trading dominates have preceded extended price declines for Bitcoin.\",\n    \"The market is showing signs of being 'overheated' with a high ratio of speculators compared to long-term holders.\",\n    \"Decrypt highlights that the surge was built on 'shaky ground', echoing the sentiment that the rally lacks fundamental support.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\n\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-risks-decline-rally-speculative-not-structural-cryptoquant\n\nPublished Time: Fri, 01 May 2026 10:28:12 GMT\n\nMarkdown Content:\n# Bitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\n\n[![Image 2: Cointelegraph](https://cointelegraph.com/_platypus/ducklings/logo.BYXtOGOo.svg)](https://cointelegraph.com/)\n\nEcosystem\n\n[](https://twitter.com/cointelegraph)[](https://telegram.me/cointelegraph)[](https://www.facebook.com/cointelegraph)[](https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCRqBu-grVX1p97WaX4d-OuQ)\n\nEnglish\n\nNews\n\n[Markets](https://cointelegraph.com/category/markets)[Features](https://cointelegraph.com/category/features)\n\nSponsored\n\nAbout\n\nLINK$9.14 0.48%\n\nBTC$77,338 1.70%\n\nXLM$0.1594 0.14%\n\nTRX$0.3254 0.08%\n\nXMR$387.28 1.37%\n\nDOGE$0.108 1.39%\n\nBCH$442.94 0.28%\n\nADA$0.2477 0.76%\n\nBNB$616.92 0.17%\n\nETH$2,283 1.05%\n\nSOL$83.98 1.19%\n\nHYPE$40.80 4.41%\n\nXRP$1.37 0.30%\n\nLINK$9.14 0.52%\n\nBTC$77,346 1.73%\n\nXLM$0.1594 0.00%\n\nTRX$0.3254 0.04%\n\nXMR$387.28 1.34%\n\nDOGE$0.1079 1.26%\n\nBCH$443.15 0.23%\n\nADA$0.2477 0.77%\n\nBNB$616.85 0.16%\n\nETH$2,284 1.07%\n\nSOL$83.97 1.18%\n\nHYPE$40.82 4.42%\n\nXRP$1.37 0.30%\n\nBitcoin Risks Decline After Futures-Driven April Rally: CryptoQuant\n\n[![Image 3: Advertisement](https://s3.cointelegraph.com/storage/uploads/view/cee55e6025824208ec57e2db3e0dd887.jpg)](https://servedbyadbutler.com/redirect.spark?MID=169476&plid=2808712&setID=351403&channelID=0&CID=1052016&banID=523258321&PID=0&textadID=0&tc=1&rnd=6205787628&scheduleID=2744665&placementScheduleId=2744665&adItemScheduleId=0&adSize=1160x65&metadata=%5B%5D&mt=1777631403368014&spr=1&referrer=https%3A%2F%2Fcointelegraph.com%2F&request_uuid=9fe220b5-6cd7-4aa4-9fe8-c4deca9726a3&hc=bec88fe47e5e2569409a713dec756f95b4aa92b2&location=)![Image 4](https://servedbyadbutler.com/adserve/;MID=169476;type=e959fb862;placementID=2808712;setID=351403;channelID=0;CID=1052016;BID=523258321;TAID=0;place=0;rnd=6205787628;psrtype=api;referrer=https%3A%2F%2Fcointelegraph.com%2F;request_uuid=9fe220b5-6cd7-4aa4-9fe8-c4deca9726a3;mt=1777631403368047;hc=9e0a07c91518e753510a225bc6386c941016fe14)![Image 5](https://servedbyadbutler.com/adserve/;MID=169476;type=v959fb862;placementID=2808712;setID=351403;channelID=0;CID=1052016;BID=523258321;TAID=0;place=0;rnd=6205787628;psrtype=api;referrer=https%3A%2F%2Fcointelegraph.com%2F;request_uuid=9fe220b5-6cd7-4aa4-9fe8-c4deca9726a3;mt=1777631403368040;hc=fb7215b196f7b2e6a87e62a384e0a0cdd97b1103)\n\n![Image 6](https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/author-images/file/author-1538-felix-ng.jpg?prefix=media%2Fauthor-images)![Image 7](https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/author-images/file/author-1510-jesse-coghlan.jpg?prefix=media%2Fauthor-images)\n\nWritten by[Jesse Coghlan](https://cointelegraph.com/authors/jesse-coghlan)⁠,  Staff Editor.Reviewed by[Felix Ng](https://cointelegraph.com/authors/felix-ng)⁠,  Staff Editor.\n\n![Image 8](https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/author-images/file/author-1510-jesse-coghlan.jpg?prefix=media%2Fauthor-images)Written by[Jesse Coghlan](https://cointelegraph.com/authors/jesse-coghlan)⁠,  Staff Editor.\n\n![Image 9](https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/author-images/file/author-1538-felix-ng.jpg?prefix=media%2Fauthor-images)Reviewed by[Felix Ng](https://cointelegraph.com/authors/felix-ng)⁠,  Staff Editor.\n\n# Bitcoin risks extended retreat as April rally was futures-driven: CryptoQuant\n\n[Latest News](https://cointelegraph.com/category/latest-news)Published May 1, 2026\n\nFutures drove up Bitcoin's price in April while spot demand declined, which CryptoQuant warned has historically preceded extended price declines.\n\n![Image 10](https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/article-covers/file/HI%20marketsPro%20one-stop%20institutional-grade%20crypto%20intelligence%20dashboard%20Bitcoin.jpg?prefix=media%2Farticle-covers)\n\nBitcoin could be setting up for a multimonth price decline, after a rally in April driven mainly by futures traders while spot demand declined, according to the crypto analytics firm CryptoQuant.\n\nBitcoin gained around 20% in April, rising from $66,000 to a peak of $79,000 in a rally “driven entirely by growth in perpetual futures demand,” CryptoQuant said in a [report](https://cryptoquant.com/insights/research/69f3805fe2872616b411be88-30-April-2026-Speculative-Rally-Bitcoins-April-Price-Surge-Was-Fueled-by-Perpetu) on Thursday.\n\nMeanwhile, spot demand for Bitcoin contracted throughout the rally, “indicating that the market’s marginal buyer was speculative, not fundamental,” it said.\n\n“The divergence between rising price and contracting spot demand is one of the clearest on-chain signals that price gains are speculative rather than structural,” CryptoQuant added.\n\nBitcoin is [trading around $77,000](https://cointelegraph.com/markets/repeat-bitcoin-profit-taking-near-77k-suggests-rally-is-loosing-steam) at the time of writing, rising 2.1% over the past 2\\n\\nTitle: Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn\n\nURL Source: https://decrypt.co/366267/bitcoin-crash-incoming-april-surge-built-shaky-ground-analysts-warn\n\nPublished Time: 2026-04-30T20:30:19\n\nMarkdown Content:\n# Bitcoin Crash Incoming? April Surge Was Built on Shaky Ground, Analysts Warn - Decrypt\n\n[![Image 1: Decrypt logo](https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/full-logo-black.svg)![Image 2: Decrypt logo](https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/full-logo-white.svg)](https://decrypt.co/)[](https://decrypt.co/gg)[](https://decrypt.co/university)[](https://decrypt.co/university)[](https://decrypt.co/emerge)\n\n[![Image 3: Decrypt logo](https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fit:3840:0:0:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/logo-mark-white.svg@webp)![Image 4: Decrypt logo](https://img.decrypt.co/insecure/rs:fit:3840:0:0:0/plain/https://cdn.decrypt.co/wp-content/themes/decrypt-media/assets/images/branding-2024/logo-mark-black.svg@webp)](https://decrypt.co/)\n\n[News](https://decrypt.co/news)[Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[GG](https://decrypt.co/gg)[Emerge](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[Videos](https://decrypt.co/videos)[Newsletters](https://decrypt.co/newsletters)\n\nEnglish\n\nSign Up[Partner with us](https://dastan.co/partner)\n\n* * *\n\n* * *\n\n[![Image 5: News](blob:http://localhost/0aa0a8ee08caf3bcc8e7e488283150b2)![Image 6: News](blob:http://localhost/9a89213175e2fb47d512c1624a349836)News](https://decrypt.co/news)[![Image 7: Predict](blob:http://localhost/83e225a6c9ce2bac8adf311c3e67de6b)![Image 8: Predict](blob:http://localhost/d3717f8b551ce4e2a9b35e1641d61392)Predict](https://myriad.markets/?utm_source=decrypt&utm_campaign=navbar)[![Image 9: AI](blob:http://localhost/62ceb084dde83843d9887bdc1213ad1f)![Image 10: AI](blob:http://localhost/7aa2f6422d5e2e5af6a262ad86bf9b91)AI](https://decrypt.co/emerge)[![Image 11: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)![Image 12: Learn](blob:http://localhost/132e5adddd21434e4b62b0d79cacaf2c)Learn](https://decrypt.co/university)[![Image 13: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/e44cea5a102a4ce9cbe1c97f51994f1b)![Image 14: Gaming](blob:http://localhost/f89fd6ac9ca89f35ed6d49f4a70a6652)Gaming](https://decrypt.co/gg)\n\n## Coin Prices\n\n### [BTC](https://decrypt.co/price/bitcoin)\n\n$77,137.00\n\n1.41%\n### [ETH](https://decrypt.co/price/ethereum)\n\n$2,277.39\n\n0.68%\n### [XRP](https://decrypt.co/price/xrp)\n\n$1.37\n\n-0.12%\n### [BNB](https://decrypt.co/price/binance-coin)\n\n$616.15\n\n-0.08%\n### [USDC](https://decrypt.co/price/usd-coin)\n\n$0.999765\n\n0.00%\n### [SOL](https://decrypt.co/price/solana)\n\n$83.77\n\n0.78%\n### [TRX](https://decrypt.co/price/tron)\n\n$0.32598\n\n-0.02%\n### [FIGR_HELOC](https://decrypt.co/price/figure-heloc)\n\n$1.031\n\n-0.24%\n### [DOGE](https://decrypt.co/price/dogecoin)\n\n$0.107465\n\n0.08%\n### [WBT](https://decrypt.co/price/whitebit)\n\n$57.80\n\n0.44%\n### [USDS](https://decrypt.co/price/usds)\n\n$0.999762\n\n0.01%\n### [HYPE](https://decrypt.co/price/hyperliquid)\n\n$40.69\n\n4.22%\n### [LEO](https://decrypt.co/price/bitfinex)\n\n$10.32\n\n-0.46%\n### [ADA](https://decrypt.co/price/cardano)\n\n$0.247395\n\n0.30%\n### [BCH](https://decrypt.co/price/bitcoin-cash)\n\n$442.13\n\n-0.81%\n### [XMR](https:/